'''''Star Wars: Maul - Shadow Lord''''' is an animated series whose [[Maul - Shadow Lord Season 1|first season]] of ten episodes was released between [[April 6]] and [[May 4]], [[2026]]. Set during the [[Imperial Era]], a few short [[Standard year|years]] after [[Order 66]],<ref name="Teaser sw.com" /> it will follow the former [[Sith]] [[Maul]] as he rebuilds his criminal empire. The show was first announced at [[Celebration Japan (2025)|''Star Wars'' Celebration Japan]], during a panel celebrating the 20th anniversary of [[Lucasfilm Animation]].<ref name="Celeb Maul" /> ''Maul - Shadow Lord'' is created by [[Dave Filoni]], and developed by Filoni and [[Matt Michnovetz]], with [[Brad Rau]] as supervising director, and produced by [[Lucasfilm Animation]]. The series features a more stylized version of the animation style from the previous animated series.<ref name="Teaser sw.com" />

A five-issue prequel [[Star Wars comic books|comic miniseries]] titled ''[[Star Wars: Shadow of Maul]]'' written by [[Benjamin Percy]] was published beginning on [[March 4]], [[2026]].<ref name="Marvel">{{Marvel|url=articles/comics/star-wars-shadow-of-maul-prequel-comic-maul-shadow-lord-animated-series|text=The 'Star Wars: Shadow of Maul' Comic Series Establishes the World of the Upcoming Animated Show}}</ref>

==Development==
{{Quote|Maul is a character that's our responsibility...George [Lucas] and I had had some talks about Maul over the years and what his plans for Maul had been. And so I felt it was a way of honoring that future that we were going to have and finally bringing some of it to light.|Dave Filoni, on the impetus for the series|<ref name="OfficialTrailer">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-trailer|text=Watch the Official Trailer for Star Wars: Maul – Shadow Lord - Updated}}</ref>}}
Reports of a [[Maul]]-focused animated series first emerged in late [[2021]].<ref name="Rumors">{{WebCite|url=https://www.cinelinx.com/movie-news/tv/new-star-wars-animated-series-to-focus-on-darth-mauls-shenanigans-exclusive|text=New Star Wars Animated Series to Focus on Darth Maul's Shenanigans &#124; Exclusive|author=[[Jordan Maison]]|date=2021-11-01|work=[https://www.cinelinx.com Cinelinx]|archivedate=20250118200540}}</ref> On [[April 18]], [[2025]], at [[Celebration Japan (2025)|''Star Wars'' Celebration Japan]], ''Star Wars: Maul - Shadow Lord'' was officially announced at [[Lucasfilm Animation]]'s panel.<ref name="Swcom Maul" /> The series is produced by [[Athena Yvette Portillo]], the head writer is [[Matt Michnovetz]]<ref name="Celeb Maul" /> and it will star [[Sam Witwer]].<ref name="Swcom Maul" /> According to Witwer, he was first brought in on the series by [[Dave Filoni]] about a year prior to the announcement.<ref name="Celeb Maul" /> A trailer was shown to those in attendance at the panel suggested the series, while broadly following the animation style pioneered by ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'', would have its own flourish.<ref name="Gizmodo Breakdown">{{WebCite|url=https://gizmodo.com/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-trailer-description-celebration-japan-2000589924|text=''Maul: Shadow Lord'' Is ''Star Wars''{{'s}} Next Animated Series|author=Sabina Graves|date=2025-04-18|archivedate=20250419181340}}</ref>

[[File:MaulStance-MaulShadowLord.png|thumb|left|300px|Footage of Maul was revealed within the twentieth anniversary of Lucasfilm Animation video.]]
The panel-exclusive trailer revealed the series would entail Maul striking against the criminal underworld as he rebuilds his power, confronting the [[Inquisitor]] [[Marrok|First Brother]] and a [[Eeko-Dio Daki|Mosyk Jedi]], and taking on a new [[Twi'lek]] [[Devon Izara|apprentice]],<ref name="Gizmodo Breakdown" /> whom he believed would help him in his quest for vengeance after he received a [[Force vision]].<ref name="TrailerTwitter">{{Twitter|username=sw_holocron|url=status/1913133176693948464|name=''Star Wars'' Holocron|date=2025-04-18|quote=A new animated series MAUL: SHADOW LORD has been announced. A first trailer was shown and depicts Maul as he navigates life between the events of The Clone Wars and Rebels. The plot seems to focus on Maul training a new padawan after having a vision she can help him seek revenge.  The trailer shows Maul fight Marrok who says, "So it's true. You live.}}</ref> The trailer also featured a small crew still serving Maul,<ref name="Mandalorians">{{Twitter|username=HarrisHarrisev9|url=status/1913135709252186434|name=HarrisHarrisev9|date=2025-04-18|quote=That Shadow Lord trailer was incredible!! Ruthless Maul and his remaining Mandalorian crew in the SW underworld! He takes on a young Apprentice too!! Ends with him fighting an Inquisitor in top a moving speeder!  I'm SO HYPED! #SWCJ}}</ref> including the [[Mandalorian]] [[Rook Kast]].<ref name="RookKast">{{Twitter|username=z_kokonut|url=status/1913180839354974222|name=z_kokonut|date=2025-04-19|quote=Rook Kast is back in Maul Shadow Lord!! I'm glad to see her return. I remember the theories about her being the armourer in Mandalorian.}}</ref> Footage of Maul from ''Shadow Lord'' was publicly showcased in a tribute video made to celebrate twenty years of [[Lucasfilm Animation]].<ref name="LucasfilmAnimation">{{SWYouTube|MUc6CHQLEyg|Lucasfilm Animation 20th Anniversary}}</ref>

On [[April 2]], [[2026]], [[StarWars.com]] announced a [[Maul - Shadow Lord Season 2|second season]] for ''Maul - Shadow Lord''.<ref name="Season 2 Announce" />

==Release and reception==
The official teaser trailer was released on [[January 22]], [[2026]]<ref name="Teaser sw.com" /> and a trailer was released on [[March 16]].<ref name="Trailer sw.com">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-trailer|text=Watch the Official Trailer for ''Star Wars: Maul – Shadow Lord''}}</ref> The [[Maul - Shadow Lord Season 1|first season]]<ref name="Season 2 Announce" /> released on [[Disney+]] between [[April 6]] and [[May 4]], 2026.<ref name="Teaser sw.com" />

==Continuity==
At Celebration Japan, Sam Witwer stated that the events of ''Maul - Shadow Lord'' occurred about a year after the [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] of the Clone Wars,<ref name="Celeb Maul" /> thereby corresponding to around the year [[18 BBY]] in the [['ABY-BBY' dating system|''Star Wars'' timeline system]] as the war ended in [[19 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''</ref> However, [[StarWars.com]] later stated the show in fact took place "in the period a few short years after Order 66",<ref name="Teaser sw.com"/> placing it in [[17 BBY]] at the earliest.<ref name="Timelines" /> This was later reiterated in other sources, which have framed the series as occuring in 17 BBY at the earliest<ref name="Meet the Castdate">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-cast|text=Meet the Cast of ''Star Wars: Maul – Shadow Lord'' - Update}} establishes that the events of ''Maul - Shadow Lord'' occur "a few [[Standard year|years]]" after the [[Proclamation of the New Order]], an event placed in [[19 BBY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Therefore, the events of ''Shadow Lord'' must occur in 17 BBY at the earliest according to this source.</ref><ref name="Triviadate">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-trivia|text=Inside the Making of ''Star Wars: Maul – Shadow Lord''}} establishes that the events of ''Maul- Shadow Lord'' occur some "[[Standard year|years]]" after Maul was introduced to [[cassius tea]] by the Mandalorian [[Pre Vizsla]], which was depicted during the events of "[[Eminence (episode)|Eminence]]". The events of "Eminence" are dated to [[19 BBY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Therefore, the events of ''Shadow Lord'' must occur in 17 BBY at the earliest according to this source.</ref><ref name="SpybotNote">{{Databank|spybot|Spybot}} establishes that the events of ''Maul- Shadow Lord'' occur some "[[Standard year|years]]" after the [[Clone Wars]], which [[Mission to Mustafar|end]] in [[19 BBY]] according to ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]''. Therefore, the events of ''Shadow Lord'' must occur in 17 BBY at the earliest according to this source.</ref> or more vaguely stated the series occurs during the "early days"<ref name="Kast DB">{{Databank|rook-kast|Rook Kast}}</ref><ref name="Eeko DB">{{Databank|eeko-dio-daki|Eeko-Dio Daki}}</ref> and "early years" of the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Trailer sw.com" /><ref name="Devon DB">{{Databank|devon-izara|Devon Izara}}</ref><ref name="Who is Maul">{{SW|url=news/who-is-maul|text=Who is Maul?}}</ref><ref name="Devious Moments">{{SW|url=news/maul-best-moments-and-essential-battles|text=Maul's Most Devious Moments}}</ref><ref name="From Spider Legs to Nightsister Magick">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-maul-shadow-lord-leg-list|text=From Spider Legs to Nightsister Magick: The Many Mechanical Limbs of Maul}}</ref><ref name="Legacy saber">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-legacy-lightsaber-devon-izara|text=Embrace your Inner Jedi with Devon Izara's Legacy Lightsaber - Reveal}}</ref>

